<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Macomer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1478</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Macomer was fought on 19 May 1478 in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-alagon">Leonardo Alagon</a>, Marquis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oristano">Oristano</a>, and the forces of the Aragonese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>. Alagon, the last great Sardinian feudal rebel, was defeated, captured and imprisoned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> until his death. His marquisate was confiscated by the crown, ending the last trace of independent power on the island.</p></div>
